# ER-OVERWATCH Lane Rules

## Directory Boundaries (NEVER CROSS THESE)
- `frontend/patient-client/`: Next.js 14, Tailwind 4, TypeScript only.
- `frontend/nurse-command/`: React 19, Vite, Tailwind 4, TypeScript only. Fall detection is **browser-side**.
- `backend/triage-engine/`: FastAPI, Python 3.11, Pydantic v2 only.
- `backend/rppg/`: Python 3.11, OpenCV, MediaPipe — rPPG only.
- `backend/scene-intel/`: **Deprecated** — do not extend.
- `shared/`: Pydantic schemas (source of truth) + TypeScript mirrors. Architect 3 owns schema changes.

Do NOT modify files outside your assigned app unless explicitly updating shared schemas.

## Fall vs rPPG
- Falls: `browserFallDetector.ts` → `POST /api/v1/alerts/fall-report`
- rPPG: patient clips → `POST /api/v1/rppg` → `backend/rppg`

## Mock First
Use mocks matching `docs/API_endpoints.md` and `shared/types/telemetry.ts`.

## LiveKit
Memoize LiveKit hooks with `useMemo`/`useCallback` to prevent infinite re-renders.
